FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:1352 — plain `STORE` refuses before checking locals, so a shadowing local still fails — contradicts `src/vm.rs:512` where `set_var` writes a live local first and only refuses a global fallthrough — fix by checking locals first / moving the refusal into `set_var` after the locals scan
2. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:758 — `BytecodeVm::set_var` has no constant refusal at all, so `SET_PROPERTY` (`src/bytecode/vm.rs:1522`) and `DEF_METHOD` outside an object (`src/bytecode/vm.rs:1739`) rebind a global constant silently while tree-walker `set_var` refuses — fix by mirroring `Vm::set_var` refusal in `BytecodeVm::set_var`/`bind`
3. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:1988 — `modules.insert` is recorded before `compile_module`/`drive`, so a failed first import stays cached and a second import in a `try`/`catch` becomes a no-op success while `src/vm.rs:379` only records after success — fix by inserting after the module runs or removing on `Err`
4. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:1849 — failure path truncates `loops` without `restore_shadowed`, so a `for each X` shadowing a constant/global leaves the loop value in `globals` after the `catch` while the success path restores at `src/bytecode/vm.rs:1451` — fix by restoring displaced bindings when truncating on `handle_failure`/`discard_frames_above`/`unwind_frame`
5. [MINOR] docs/BYTECODE.md:172 — row says `NOP` arg is `END_TRY_MARKER` or `0`, but `src/bytecode/vm.rs:1013` treats any `arg != END_TRY_MARKER` as filler — fix doc to say only the marker closes a region, every other value is filler
